\hat{m}_t = D_\psi(y_{t-k:t}, q_t)

Semantic mapping (new in v0.7). How does an LLM memory item become  m ? The LLM produces an embedding  e \in \mathbb{R}^{d_e} . A learned compressor  \pi: \mathbb{R}^{d_e} \to \mathbb{R}^{d_m}  maps to the chemical input space, with  d_m  bounded by  C_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\mathrm{idle}} . The compressor is trained jointly with  E_\phi  under the bit-budget constraint. Without this, the "learned" claim is unsupported.

