17. Core Scientific Proposition

\text{LLM} + \text{learned interface} + \text{physical dynamical memory} + \text{digital provenance}

with the information pathway:

m \xrightarrow{E_\phi} u \xrightarrow{F_{\mathrm{unknown}}} x \xrightarrow{H} y \xrightarrow{D_\psi} \hat{m}

and the hybrid memory:

M = M_D + M_C

The research question is whether:

P(M_D^{\mathrm{matched}} + M_C) > P(M_D^{\mathrm{matched}})

under controlled conditions and for a clearly defined class of long-horizon associative-memory tasks in the idle regime.

