Appendix I — Open Theoretical Questions

1. Optimal spectral design for idle memory. What eigenvalue distribution maximizes  I(m; y_\Delta)  subject to ESP constraints? Formally, solve:

\max_{\{\lambda_i\}} I(m; y_\Delta) \quad \text{s.t.} \quad |\lambda_i| < 1, \quad \mathrm{MC} = N

2. Trade-off between nonlinearity and retention. Is there a fundamental bound on  \mathrm{IPC} \cdot \tau_{\mathrm{idle}}  for a given reservoir dimension? Conjecture:

\mathrm{IPC} \cdot \tau_{\mathrm{idle}} \leq C(N)

for some function  C(N) .

3. Information-theoretic capacity of chemical channels. What is the exact form of  C_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\mathrm{idle}}(\Delta)  for a well-mixed CRN with mass-action kinetics? Conjecture: it is bounded by the rank of the steady-state Jacobian.
4. Attractor design for content-addressable memory. How many patterns can be stored in a chemical attractor network with  N  species and  R  reactions? Conjecture:  M \leq \alpha N / \log N  for some constant  \alpha , analogous to Hopfield capacity.
5. Copy-number noise limits. How does  C_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\mathrm{idle}}(\Delta)  scale with system volume  \Omega ? Conjecture:  C_{\mathrm{eff}}^{\mathrm{idle}} \sim \log \Omega  for large  \Omega .
6. Phase transitions in memory capacity. Does the memory capacity exhibit a sharp transition as a function of reservoir parameters (e.g., spectral radius, nonlinearity)? Conjecture: a transition at the edge of chaos, analogous to the critical line in ESNs.
7. Universality of the forgetting tension. Is the tension between ESP and idle memory fundamental, or can it be circumvented by designed non-normal dynamics? Conjecture: non-normal dynamics can transiently amplify memory but cannot circumvent the asymptotic bound.
8. Chemical implementation of attention. Can a chemical reaction network implement a softmax-like attention mechanism? If so, what is the capacity scaling?

